<title>NEW ZEALAND: LION TAKES OVER STELLA DISTRIBUTION IN NZ.</title>
<headline>LION TAKES OVER STELLA DISTRIBUTION IN NZ.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australasian brewer Lion Nathan Ltd said on Thursday it had taken over the distribution in New Zealand of Belgium's Stella Artois beer from its 50 percent owned subsidiary NZ Wines and Spirits.</p>
<p>Lion said the move would enhance its portfolio of premium brands.</p>
<p>&quot;The new distribution arrangement is part of Lion Breweries' commitment to grow our leadership of the premium category as consumers continue to move up from quantity to quality and demand more choice,&quot; Lion managing director Kevin Stratful said in a statement.  </p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom +64 4 4714 272</p>
